# Native signed TEST procedure integration v1

This is a new prospective integration of the exact surviving saved candidate in
`../results/cold_synthesis-prime.json`, `synthesis.candidate_artifacts[0]`. Its
procedure bytes must equal the saved successful procedure and its native
counterexample-set CID must rederive from the saved synthesis counterexamples.
The source catalog and all native sources are unchanged. Original episode
identifiers are retained as legacy aliases with exact saved source/artifact
bindings; they are not silently converted into newly executed episodes.

Before new evaluation, the complete scripts, source identities, fresh input
corpora, evidence contracts, key commitment and runtime identities are frozen.
New test, adversarial, held-out and shadow inputs are disjoint from the original
training and exposed query pool. They are authored after the original
development and held apart for this integration only; they are not a recruited
population or evidence of generalization beyond this bounded task.

The proof producer asks Z3 whether the selected operation-contract conjunction
differs from an independently encoded bounded sequence decision specification,
for lengths zero through six, supported JSON value classes, bounded integer
values and budgets. It preserves SMT statements and solver results. A separate
concrete bridge checks the actual frozen catalog and selected graph on the
declared finite corpus. This is a proof of the explicit symbolic decision
contract plus measured source bridge; it is not a theorem for arbitrary Python
or a proof that an asserted receipt is true merely because it has a CID.

Separate concrete test, adversarial, held-out and pre-certificate shadow
evaluators run the saved candidate graph, retain individual observed results
and compare an independent predicate. The admission adapter verifies the actual
artifact bytes, source/input/contract identities, complete result coverage and
computed results before constructing native `AdmittedReceipt` values. It
rechecks the proof statements/results and rejects missing, changed, stale or
cross-kind artifacts. No unconditional successful evidence producer is used.

A locally generated test-only HMAC key, held outside published evidence,
instantiates the native signer registry in nonproduction mode. Native
`ProcedureVerifier`, `ProcedureCertificateIssuer` and
`ProcedureCertificateVerifier` consume the evidence in that order. All runtime
certificate and authority admission is restricted to TEST/read-only execution;
LIVE admission is rejected. No registry promotion or production authority is
created. An immutable test selection receipt occupies the explicit runtime
registry-revision binding without being called a promoted native registry.

Each public query is an immutable content-addressed artifact. A separate
canonical JSON text field preserves exact concrete float inputs, because native
canonical structured values exclude floats. READ_STATE returns the immutable
query CID descriptor; concrete check handlers resolve and validate its exact
bound JSON bytes before catalog execution. No adversarial value is dropped.
A separate
authority record binds it to exact procedure/certificate/source/policy/scope and
test mode. The native invocation commits that authority CID; its exact CID is
then mapped to the immutable record before execution. The no-input READ_STATE
handler resolves only that exact invocation mapping. It never reads an unbound
global query. Query corruption, substitution or cross-invocation reuse rejects.

Six concrete typed handlers preserve the saved contracts: read state, selected
tests, static analysis, type checking, postcondition and receipt emission.
Operation completion is distinct from the computed decision. False decisions
can be correct completed computations. Independent native observation,
validation and postcondition admission checks current-invocation receipts and
all three check values; it does not rely on the saved postcondition's single
test-result input to imply the other checks ran. The procedure causes no
filesystem/network/model effects. Immutable diagnostic artifacts are persisted
by the surrounding harness after read-only execution.

The run has a fixed outer process limit, per-invocation native resource limits,
actual bounded local isolation/budget reservations, native idempotency and
checkpoint stores. Every attempted invocation, positive/negative control,
process timing and terminal disposition is retained. Provider calls and model
tokens are zero. Signing, runtime execution and native receipts establish this
specific integration only. External promotion-gate evidence and native registry
promotion remain a separate open layer.
